From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Ballard <tom.ballard08@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:34:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pci: apple,t8010-pcie: Allow the two-port T7000

The A8 (T7000) apcie has two root ports (ADT #ports = 2), where the A8X
(T7001) has four: there are no port2 and port3 register windows or
interrupts to describe. Accept the config, rc, port0 and port1 windows
and two port interrupts for apple,t7000-pcie. The T8010, T8015 and S8003
keep their own lower bounds.

The driver maps only the windows and interrupts of the ports it uses,
so it needs no change.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
index f6497a4e1..bf96da5b1 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
@@ -29,7 +29,8 @@ description: |
   Apple A8/A8X (T7000/T7001) devices use an earlier version of the same root
   complex, with the same ECAM layout, port register block and MSI block. It
   has no separate PHY register windows and no NVMMU, and its reference and
-  auxiliary clocks are power domains.
+  auxiliary clocks are power domains. The A8 has two root ports and the A8X
+  four, each with its register window and interrupt.
 
   Each enabled root port is represented by a child node. This allows port
   devices to carry their own reset, clock-request, firmware and other
@@ -46,8 +47,10 @@ allOf:
     then:
       properties:
         reg:
+          minItems: 4
           maxItems: 6
         reg-names:
+          minItems: 4
           items:
             - const: config
             - const: rc
@@ -56,8 +59,10 @@ allOf:
             - const: port2
             - const: port3
         interrupts:
+          minItems: 2
           maxItems: 4
         interrupt-names:
+          minItems: 2
           maxItems: 4
         power-domains:
           items:
@@ -152,22 +157,22 @@ properties:
           - const: apple,t8010-pcie
 
   reg:
-    minItems: 6
+    minItems: 4
     maxItems: 9
 
   reg-names:
-    minItems: 6
+    minItems: 4
     maxItems: 9
 
   interrupts:
     description:
       One state interrupt for each root port followed, on the SoCs with a
       storage-port NVMMU, by its fault interrupt.
-    minItems: 4
+    minItems: 2
     maxItems: 5
 
   interrupt-names:
-    minItems: 4
+    minItems: 2
     items:
       - const: port0
       - const: port1
